    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="1452" n="1418" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg1418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Vienna Legation Files: Lot 54F57: Box 565:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-15T20:00:00+01:00">April 15, 1948—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>485. From Keyes and Yost. We strongly endorse proposed joint approach to Moscow
                    concerning Berlin and Vienna situation (Department’s 345 April 14<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d776-f1"/>). We consider approach should be made at earliest
                    possible moment in hope that it may prevent Soviets from imposing further
                    restrictive measures which, once taken, they might find difficult to
                    withdraw.</p>
                <p>Our only suggestions re text of communication aré following: (1) that in view of
                    increasing Soviet pressure here, Vienna be associated with Berlin in opening
                    sentence and throughout text wherever appropriate, rather than being mentioned
                    only in penultimate paragraph; (2) that a new penultimate paragraph be added
                    referring to guarantee contained in 1945 EAC Agreement of “free and unimpeded
                    access” from Vienna to Allied airdromes at Tulln and Schwechat, since separation
                    of these airdromes from Vienna zones of occupation represents vital
                    communications factor which does not obtain in Berlin. Recently imposed Soviet
                    restriction on traffic to and from these airdromes emphasizes importance of our
                    dealing with this point immediately.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 485, repeated Berlin 31, Moscow 13. [Keyes and Yost.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Yost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
